== WHAT THIS LOG DEMONSTRATES ==
   Casting 10 narrowed VERIFIER_PATH_PATTERNS and moved every derived run
   table into foundry_state. Both reach modules casting 10 does not own, so
   this log drives those peer modules and records that they still pass. All
   four are peer-owned: test_inspect_mode.py is casting 12's,
   tests/orchestration/ is casting 2's, test_measure_run.py is casting 3's,
   test_lead_prose.py is the lead-protocol pin. The SCOPE is deliberately wide
   for that reason -- narrowing it to a frozen node-id roster would buy
   stability by giving up the cross-casting non-interference claim this log
   exists to carry.

== WHY THIS BODY PRINTS A VERDICT AND NOT A COUNT (the C-101 ruling) ==
   The fragility is PEER-OWNERSHIP, not counting. Every module above belongs
   to another casting, so any number this body derives from the population is
   moved by work this log never ran and its owner never sees. Measured at
   438de87 against the committed body: 1282 -> 1303 passed, every progress-dot
   line and percentage shifted, and the two test_module_boundaries.py skip
   line numbers drifted 6650 -> 6768 and 6698 -> 6816. Three moving numbers,
   none of them a claim. Three repairs were weighed; two are rejected here, on
   the record, so the next cycle does not rediscover this as an open question.

   REJECTED -- declare the count volatile. Inadmissible at the door, not
   merely undesirable. evidence.py#_erased_disagreement_problem (D-135)
   refuses a redaction reconciling a real disagreement, and a 1282-to-1303
   span classifies against no member of evidence.py#_ENVIRONMENTAL_GRAMMARS:
   a count is what the command REPORTED, not where it RAN. It also repairs
   none of the dot lines or the skip line numbers.

   REJECTED -- select by explicit node id. It stops the drift by narrowing the
   CLAIM rather than the output: the nodes named on the day the command is
   typed become the whole of what the log asserts, so a peer test added next
   cycle falls silently outside a body still read as non-interference
   assurance. It also leaves the skip line numbers drifting, and those cannot
   be dropped -- see the roster note below.

   ADOPTED -- keep the SCOPE exactly as it was, all four modules still
   running, and derive the body. The verdict below carries the exit code, the
   FAILED/ERROR lines and a collected floor, in the spelling
   evidence/casting-1-no-degradation.log and
   evidence/casting-4-temper-candidate.log already ship. A floor is a constant
   in the body, so it never disagrees and never needs a volatile declaration,
   and it fails CLOSED where a bare PASS/FAIL fails open.
   1250 is the floor because it sits above what would remain if any ONE of the
   four modules vanished from the selection. Collected at 438de87: 1314 total
   = 174 test_inspect_mode + 799 tests/orchestration + 83 test_measure_run +
   258 test_lead_prose. The largest survivor of a single-module loss is
   1314 - 83 = 1231, below 1250, so losing a whole module cannot report MET.
   Growth never trips a floor; only removal does, and a trip is an alarm worth
   reading. Raise it deliberately when the population grows.

== WHY THE SKIP ROSTER KEEPS ITS PATHS AND DROPS ITS LINE NUMBERS ==
   evidence.py#_ENVIRONMENTAL_GRAMMARS names THIS log, by name, as the live
   corpus witness for planning_root and archive_root. The sweep in
   test_evidence.py#_corpus_witness_fields_by_log applies this log's OWN
   volatile declarations to this log's OWN body and asks whether a token of
   each shape is erased. The two paths in the roster below ARE those tokens.
   A tidier verdict-only body with no roster would leave both grammars
   declared and unwitnessed and turn
   test_evidence.py#test_every_declared_grammar_has_a_live_witness red -- which
   is why the roster stays and why the checkout root inside it is left
   unfolded on purpose. The pytest session header is kept for the same reason:
   it is what the platform, rootdir and plugins declarations erase, and
   evidence.py cites this log's platform declaration by name.
   The LINE NUMBERS are stripped instead. They address sibling castings'
   files and they drifted without one line of casting 10's work changing. A
   line number is the one part of a skip line that carries no claim and no
   witness.

== NOTHING IS DESELECTED, AND THE SELECTION IS WHOLE ==
   Four tests/test_inspect_mode.py nodes were deselected here as RED at
   d1e27ea under concern C-071 against casting 12. They PASS at 438de87, so
   the deselects are gone and the whole module is driven. That also retires
   the deselected count, which was the third moving number in this body.

